---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES | Sign-Flip Street Culture, Grime Art & XRP KIDs Lore"
  description="NO BALL GAMES turns restricted-space signage into a street-culture system spanning Charlie Buster's Grime Art visual language and the XRP KIDs lore branch."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-card hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Sign flip • Grime Art • XRP canon</span>
      <h1>NO BALL <span class="hero-title-accent">GAMES</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The sign said no. The culture played anyway. This public site now carries the core truth pillars directly: restricted-space rebellion, Charlie Buster's Grime Art backbone, and the XRP KIDs internal canon branch.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}projects/`}>Explore project lanes</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}research/`}>Open truth sources</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-grid" aria-label="Core pillars">
        <div class="stat"><strong>NO BALL GAMES</strong><span>sign-flip street identity</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>Grime Art</strong><span>raw UK visual language</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>XRP KIDs</strong><span>100 / 89 / 11 canon</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-card hero-sign" aria-label="NO BALL GAMES sign graphic">
      <div class="restricted-board">
        <strong>NO BALL</strong>
        <strong>GAMES</strong>
        <span>Play anyway</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        From estate walls and blocked courts to painted clothing, collector drops and chain-side myth. One name, multiple lanes, clear truth labels.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Three main pillars</h2>
      <p>Each pillar has its own role so culture, art and lore do not get blurred.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">01 • NO BALL GAMES</span>
        <h3>Restricted-space rebellion</h3>
        <p>
          British warning signage, locked courts, fenced spaces and estate memory become the central brand language. Restriction is flipped into ownership, community and creative defiance.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}about/`}>Read the brand story →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">02 • Charlie Buster / Grime Art</span>
        <h3>Raw UK visual backbone</h3>
        <p>
          Grime Art is presented as the street-rooted visual layer: graffiti texture, portrait energy, painted clothing and one-of-one work. Historical and collaboration claims stay source-safe.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}about/`}>See the artist layer →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">03 • XRP NO BALL GAMES</span>
        <h3>XRP KIDs lore branch</h3>
        <p>
          Internal canon includes XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG. Treat this as lore unless issuer, collection and ledger records are verified.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Enter the XRP branch →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Canon anchors</span>
      <h2>What the XRP branch carries.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>100 genesis XRP KIDs at the start of the canon timeline.</li>
        <li>89 captured under Alpha Aaron's control arc.</li>
        <li>11 free KIDs forming the resistance core.</li>
        <li>FRET (Fresh Rapid Elite Team) as the Barbican-rooted response network.</li>
        <li>$PMSL as a hard-fork shield concept in the lore layer.</li>
        <li>Block Buster OG as hidden archive/memory intervention.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}lore/`}>Read lore framing →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Claim discipline</span>
      <h2>Streetwise, but proof-aware.</h2>
      <p>
        Public pages use internal canon, source-needed and verification language to avoid fake certainty. Wallet addresses, token supply numbers, market caps, floor prices and sale claims must be verified before publication.
      </p>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Verify issuer • Verify collection • Not financial advice</div>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>See truth files and rights notes →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Move through the lanes</span>
      <h2>Art. Wearables. Lore. Community.</h2>
      <p>Go deeper through projects, collections, XRP canon, community submissions and source-backed research.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}collections/`}>View collections</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
